      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We present the case of a 16-year-old boy presented with two weeks episode of worsening lower abdominal pain. Clinically, there was a tender palpable mass on the suprapubic region. Ultrasonography showed an absent spleen at its usual area, instead might represent the suprapubic mass. An emergency laparotomy revealed a congested spleen in the pelvic cavity. Splenectomy was undertaken as it was non-viable. The patient was discharged uneventfully with triple vaccinations. We describe this unique entity with its literature review."},
